mode: "100644"
text: "# Examples — voice extraction, end to end\n\nTwo contrasting walk-throughs showing the full path: sample → analysis → fingerprint →\ngenerated post. They demonstrate the *level of specificity* to aim for and that the method\nworks across very different voices. Samples are illustrative.\n\n---\n\n## Example A — a blunt, dry indie founder\n\n### Sample (real-ish input)\n> \"Spent 6 months building a feature nobody asked for. Classic. Talked to 4 customers last\n> week — turns out they wanted the boring thing I kept skipping. So I shipped the boring thing\n> in two days. It's already my most-used feature. Build less. Ask more. I'm slow to learn this.\"\n\n### Analysis (selected observations, with evidence)\n- **Lexicon:** plain, always contracts (\"nobody,\" \"it's,\" \"I'm\"). Concrete (\"6 months,\" \"4\n  customers,\" \"two days\"). Bans hype entirely.\n- **Syntax:** short declaratives, frequent fragments (\"Classic.\" \"Build less. Ask more.\").\n  One-word and two-word sentences for emphasis.\n- **Rhetoric:** self-deprecating (\"I'm slow to learn this\"), builds by contrast (months of\n  wrong work vs two days of right work), lands on a terse imperative.\n- **Structure:** confession → turn → lesson. Opens mid-story, no preamble.\n- **Stance:** peer, vulnerable, anti-overbuilding. Shares failure openly.\n- **Negative space:** no exclamation marks, no emoji, no buzzwords, no \"I'm excited to.\"\n\n### Fingerprint\n1. Opens mid-story with a blunt confession, no setup.\n2. Short sentences and deliberate fragments for emphasis.\n3. Concrete numbers in almost every post.\n4. Self-deprecating; the joke is always on himself.\n5. Lands on a 2–4 word imperative (\"Build less. Ask more.\").\n- **Never:** exclamation marks, emoji, hype words, humble-brags.\n\n### Generated post (new topic: hiring)\n> \"Hired for a résumé. Fired three months later. The résumé was great. The work wasn't.\n> Started hiring for a paid trial project instead — watch them do the actual job for a week.\n> Hit rate went way up. Stop reading résumés. Watch people work.\"\n\n→ Hits every signature; reads plausibly like the source. ✅\n\n---\n\n## Example B — a warm, encouraging service brand (a bookkeeping studio)\n\n### Sample (real-ish input)\n> \"Tax season can feel like a wall of dread — we get it. Here's the good news: you don't have\n> to face it alone, and you definitely don't have to understand every form. That's literally\n> our job. This week, just gather your receipts in one folder. That's it. One small step, and\n> we'll handle the scary parts together.\"\n\n### Analysis (selected observations, with evidence)\n- **Lexicon:** warm, reassuring (\"we get it,\" \"the good news,\" \"together\"). Plain, contracts.\n  \"Scary parts\" — names the emotion plainly.\n- **Syntax:** medium, flowing sentences; gentle. Em-dashes for warmth (\"dread — we get it\").\n- **Rhetoric:** direct address throughout (\"you don't have to…\"), reassurance pattern\n  (acknowledge fear → relieve it), one tiny actionable step.\n- **Structure:** empathy → reassurance → one small ask. Always ends with a doable next step.\n- **Stance:** mentor/ally, warm, low-pressure, \"we're in this with you.\"\n- **Negative space:** no jargon, no pressure/urgency tactics, no fear-mongering, not cutesy.\n\n### Fingerprint\n1. Opens by naming the reader's feeling (\"can feel like a wall of dread\").\n2. Pivots to reassurance with a \"good news\" / \"you don't have to\" move.\n3. Direct address throughout — warm and personal.\n4. Ends with exactly one small, doable step.\n5. Em-dashes for a gentle, spoken rhythm.\n- **Never:** jargon, urgency/pressure tactics, fear-mongering, cutesy tone.\n\n### Generated post (new topic: quarterly estimated taxes)\n> \"Quarterly taxes sneaking up on you? Take a breath — this one's smaller than it looks. You\n> don't need to calculate anything tonight. The only thing to do this week is forward us your\n> Q2 income total. We'll do the math and tell you the exact number to pay. One email from you,\n> and the rest is handled.\"\n\n→ Hits every signature; warm, low-pressure, ends on one step. ✅\n\n---\n\n## The takeaway\n\nTwo opposite voices, same method: observe with evidence, distill a falsifiable fingerprint,\nnail the negative space, then prove it by generating on a new topic. If your generated post on\na fresh topic reads like the source, the `voice.md` is doing its job. If it doesn't, the rules\naren't specific enough yet — go back to the layers.\n"
